\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {28.1.2}Comparing two trees -- and the shared-table trap}{1662}{subsection.28.1.2}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {28.1.1}{\ignorespaces \(R'\), the unrooted twin of \(R\), constructed \emph  {by definition}: apply the renaming \(\sigma =(1\tmspace  +\thickmuskip {.2777em}2\tmspace  +\thickmuskip {.2777em}5)\) (cycle \(1\DOTSB \mapstochar \rightarrow 2,\,2\DOTSB \mapstochar \rightarrow 5,\,5\DOTSB \mapstochar \rightarrow 1\), all other vertices fixed) to every edge of \(R\): \(1\!-\!2\DOTSB \mapstochar \rightarrow 2\!-\!5\)✓, \(1\!-\!3\DOTSB \mapstochar \rightarrow 2\!-\!3\)✓, \(1\!-\!4\DOTSB \mapstochar \rightarrow 2\!-\!4\)✓, \(2\!-\!5\DOTSB \mapstochar \rightarrow 5\!-\!1\)✓, \(2\!-\!6\DOTSB \mapstochar \rightarrow 5\!-\!6\)✓, \(3\!-\!7\DOTSB \mapstochar \rightarrow 3\!-\!7\)✓, \(3\!-\!8\DOTSB \mapstochar \rightarrow 3\!-\!8\)✓, \(4\!-\!9\DOTSB \mapstochar \rightarrow 4\!-\!9\)✓ -- exactly the listed edge set. A twin built as \(\sigma (R)\) needs no re-derivation: \(\sigma \) \emph  {is} the witnessed isomorphism. Yet \emph  {rooted} labels at vertex 1 disagree: \(R\) at root 1 has name \(4\); labelling \(R'\) at root 1 (rooting gives \(1\!\to \!5\!\to \!\{2,6\}\), \(2\!\to \!\{3,4\}\), \(3\!\to \!\{7,8\}\), \(4\!\to \!9\); postorder \(6,7,8,3,9,4,2,5,1\), on \(R\)'s table): leaves \(6,7,8,9\to \mathrm  {cl}=1\); \(3\to (1,1)\to \mathrm  {cl}=2\) and \(4\to (1)\to \mathrm  {cl}=3\), both \textbf  {recalled}; then \(2\to (2,3)\to \) \textbf  {fresh} \(\mathrm  {cl}=\mathbf  {5}\); \(5\to (1,5)\to \) fresh \(\mathrm  {cl}=\mathbf  {6}\); root \(1\to (6)\to \) fresh \(\mathrm  {cl}=\mathbf  {7}\). \(R'\)'s root wears \(7\ne  4\). Same unrooted tree, different rooted shape -- because \(R'\)'s vertex 1 is \(R\)'s vertex \(\sigma ^{-1}(1)=5\), a leaf, now wearing the root's hat. The verdicts 28.3 will print: rooted-at-given-1 \textbf  {NO}, centre-rooted (\(R\)'s centre 1, \(R'\)'s centre 2) \textbf  {YES}.}}{1663}{figure.caption.282}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:c22-twin}{{28.1.1}{1663}{\(R'\), the unrooted twin of \(R\), constructed \emph {by definition}: apply the renaming \(\sigma =(1\;2\;5)\) (cycle \(1\mapsto 2,\,2\mapsto 5,\,5\mapsto 1\), all other vertices fixed) to every edge of \(R\): \(1\!-\!2\mapsto 2\!-\!5\)✓, \(1\!-\!3\mapsto 2\!-\!3\)✓, \(1\!-\!4\mapsto 2\!-\!4\)✓, \(2\!-\!5\mapsto 5\!-\!1\)✓, \(2\!-\!6\mapsto 5\!-\!6\)✓, \(3\!-\!7\mapsto 3\!-\!7\)✓, \(3\!-\!8\mapsto 3\!-\!8\)✓, \(4\!-\!9\mapsto 4\!-\!9\)✓ -- exactly the listed edge set. A twin built as \(\sigma (R)\) needs no re-derivation: \(\sigma \) \emph {is} the witnessed isomorphism. Yet \emph {rooted} labels at vertex 1 disagree: \(R\) at root 1 has name \(4\); labelling \(R'\) at root 1 (rooting gives \(1\!\to \!5\!\to \!\{2,6\}\), \(2\!\to \!\{3,4\}\), \(3\!\to \!\{7,8\}\), \(4\!\to \!9\); postorder \(6,7,8,3,9,4,2,5,1\), on \(R\)'s table): leaves \(6,7,8,9\to \mathrm {cl}=1\); \(3\to (1,1)\to \mathrm {cl}=2\) and \(4\to (1)\to \mathrm {cl}=3\), both \textbf {recalled}; then \(2\to (2,3)\to \) \textbf {fresh} \(\mathrm {cl}=\mathbf {5}\); \(5\to (1,5)\to \) fresh \(\mathrm {cl}=\mathbf {6}\); root \(1\to (6)\to \) fresh \(\mathrm {cl}=\mathbf {7}\). \(R'\)'s root wears \(7\ne 4\). Same unrooted tree, different rooted shape -- because \(R'\)'s vertex 1 is \(R\)'s vertex \(\sigma ^{-1}(1)=5\), a leaf, now wearing the root's hat. The verdicts 28.3 will print: rooted-at-given-1 \textbf {NO}, centre-rooted (\(R\)'s centre 1, \(R'\)'s centre 2) \textbf {YES}}{figure.caption.282}{}}
